{"availability":"available","full":"Infinitive/Groove","name":"Groove","description":"A private, local-first vinyl collection registry, listening journal, discovery engine, and collection intelligence system.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-06T03:32:37Z","updated":"2026-10-13T01:49:43Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://infinitive.github.io/Groove/","topics":["collection-management","indexeddb","local-first","music-library","offline-first","personal-library","pwa","react","typescript","vinyl","vinyl-collection","vite"],"demo":"https://infinitive.github.io/Groove/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T20:14:46.621Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T20:14:46.621Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T20:14:46.621Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.308Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T19:31:27.845Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T20:14:46.621Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A private, local-first record shop for one man's vinyl collection.","Every serious collection deserves a proper back room — somewhere to log what's been played, chase down a pressing detail, and figure out what's been gathering dust. Groove is that back room for a physical vinyl collection: a mobile-first Progressive Web App that catalogues the shelf, journals the listens, and tells you the truth about both.","The records stay on the shelf. Groove never streams or plays audio — it's the registry, journal, and intelligence layer that sits on top of the physical collection: what's owned, what's been spun, how it graded out, and what's worth pulling next."],"features":["What do I actually own, and how complete is that record of it?","Which artists, genres, and decades dominate the shelf?","What have I never played? What have I played to death?","What's highly rated but neglected?","What should I put on next — with an actual